    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d431">

                <pb facs="0586" n="484" sameAs="frus:frus1919v01/pg484"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/2408: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Reinsch</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-09-07T19:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">September 7,
                                1919, 7 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received
                            September 8, 4.20 a.m.</hi>]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Your cipher telegram of August 27, 4 p.m.</p>
                <p>In committing itself as suggested the Chinese Government would arouse bitter
                    hostility of Japanese and pro-Japanese faction. Desperate financial condition of
                    the Government is known to you. They would fear worst consequences unless I
                    could assure them that they may actually count on financial support either by
                    way of a response to their <hi rendition="#italic">demarche</hi> made in June by
                    telegram of June 11, p.m.,<anchor n="55" xml:id="d431-f1"/> or by completing the
                    Chicago bank loan.<anchor n="56" xml:id="d431-f2"/> Latter option expressly held
                    open awaiting Chinese consent to certain conditions which the Chinese Government
                    is now ready to meet.</p>
                <p>Second difficulty: Attempt to obtain immediate acceptance in principle of
                    consortium terms will find Chinese, still suffering from many disappointments,
                    reluctant to adopt sweeping terms apart from actual loan negotiations. If it
                    were possible to give immediate assistance in one of the above alternatives,
                    negotiations for more <pb facs="0587" n="485" xml:id="pg485"/> extensive
                    arrangements would bring the results desired as a consequence of the influence
                    established by such action.</p>
                <p>I shall do everything that is safe to secure action desired. If it should be
                    necessary to define industrial loans could they be limited to communications and
                    conservancy matters?</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Reinsch</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
